<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;KANSAS CITY SOUTHERN DEPOT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kansas City Southern Depot is a historic train station, often referred to as a depot, located in various cities across Louisiana, including Zwolle, Many, and DeQuincy. It served as a crucial transportation hub for the region."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENGINE #553&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Engine #553 is a railroad engine built in 1913, part of the KCS Railroad fleet."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENGINE #1008&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Engine #1008 is a railroad engine built in 1900, part of the KCS Railroad fleet."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KCS RAILROAD DIVISION OFFICES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KCS Railroad Division Offices are located at the NE corner of 7th &amp; Michigan, serving as administrative offices."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PITTSBURG DIAMOND JUBILEE SOUVENIR PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pittsburg Diamond Jubilee Souvenir Program includes photos of KCS Railroad properties taken in 1951."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KCS RAILROAD FREIGHT DEPOT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KCS Railroad Freight Depot is located at the SE corner of 6th &amp; Locust, serving as a freight handling facility."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KCS RAILROAD PASSENGER DEPOT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KCS Railroad Passenger Depot is located at the NE corner of 7th &amp; Michigan, serving as a passenger handling facility."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KCS RAILROAD YARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KCS Railroad Yard is located at 804 East 23rd, serving as a maintenance and storage area for railroad equipment."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISSOURI RIVER TOWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Missouri River Town is a reference to a town along the Missouri River, possibly a stop for the railroad."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATCHISON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Atchison is mentioned as a city that profited from trade with Denver and the Mormon Valley."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DENVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Denver is mentioned as a destination for trade, particularly with the Mormon Valley."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORMON VALLEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mormon Valley is mentioned as a source of trade for Atchison, contributing significantly to its growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A. S. PARKER &amp; CO.&quot; &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A. S. Parker &amp; Co. is a commission house that became prominent during the period."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;D. W. ADAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"D. W. Adams is another commission house that became prominent during the period."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITY COUNCIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"City Council is the governing body of the city, mentioned as grasping for recognition."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KCS RAILROAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KCS Railroad is the primary railroad company mentioned in the text, operating various depots, yards, and engines."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMISSION BUSINESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Commission Business refers to transactions that are not direct sales but involve commissions, which contributed to the growth of Atchison."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIRECT SALE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Direct Sale refers to transactions that are straightforward sales, contrasted with commission business."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DENVER AND INDIAN TRADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Denver and Indian Trade refers to the trade route that Atchison benefited from, particularly with the Mormon Valley."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORMON VALLEY TRADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mormon Valley Trade refers to the trade that significantly increased the commerce for Atchison."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAGONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wagons are mentioned as a means of transportation used in the trade with the Mormon Valley."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAMOND JUBILEE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diamond Jubilee refers to a celebration or commemoration, likely the source of the Souvenir Program."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FREIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Freight refers to goods transported by the railroad, specifically mentioned in relation to the Freight Depot."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PASSENGER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Passenger refers to people transported by the railroad, specifically mentioned in relation to the Passenger Depot."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yard refers to the maintenance and storage area for railroad equipment, specifically mentioned in relation to the KCS Railroad Yard."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTORICAL CONTEXT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Historical Context refers to the period and events surrounding the development of the railroad and related businesses."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984</data>
    </node>
